## 2. `andThen(config)` — Sequential Function Step

**Source:** `src/workflow/steps/and-then.ts`

```ts
function andThen<INPUT, DATA, RESULT, SUSPEND_DATA, RESUME_DATA>(
  config: WorkflowStepFuncConfig<INPUT, DATA, RESULT, SUSPEND_DATA, RESUME_DATA>
): WorkflowStepFunc<INPUT, DATA, RESULT, SUSPEND_DATA, RESUME_DATA>
```

### Config shape (simplified)

```ts
{
  id: string;             // required
  name?: string;
  purpose?: string;
  retries?: number;
  inputSchema?: z.ZodTypeAny;   // override data type for this step
  outputSchema?: z.ZodTypeAny;  // constrain return type
  suspendSchema?: z.ZodTypeAny; // step-level suspend data shape
  resumeSchema?: z.ZodTypeAny;  // step-level resume data shape
  execute: (context: WorkflowExecuteContext<INPUT, DATA, SUSPEND_DATA, RESUME_DATA>) => Promise<RESULT>;
}
```

### `WorkflowExecuteContext` (available inside every `execute`)

```ts
interface WorkflowExecuteContext<INPUT, DATA, SUSPEND_DATA, RESUME_DATA> {
  data: DATA;                    // current pipeline data (output of previous step)
  state: WorkflowStepState<INPUT>; // immutable workflow-level state (userId, conversationId, …)
  workflowState: WorkflowStateStore;   // mutable key/value bag shared by all steps
  setWorkflowState(update: WorkflowStateUpdater): void;
  getStepData(stepId: string): WorkflowStepData | undefined;
  getStepResult<T>(stepId: string): T | null;
  getInitData<T>(): T;           // returns original workflow input
  suspend(reason?: string, suspendData?: SUSPEND_DATA): Promise<never>;
  bail(result?: WORKFLOW_RESULT): never; // early exit with a result
  abort(): never;
  resumeData?: RESUME_DATA;
  retryCount?: number;
  logger: Logger;
  writer: WorkflowStreamWriter;  // emit custom stream events
}
```

### Chain method signature (on `WorkflowChain`)

```ts
andThen<NEW_DATA>(config: {
  execute: (context: WorkflowExecuteContext<...>) => Promise<NEW_DATA>;
  id: string;
  name?: string;
  purpose?: string;
  retries?: number;
  inputSchema?: z.ZodTypeAny;
  outputSchema?: z.ZodTypeAny;
  suspendSchema?: z.ZodTypeAny;
  resumeSchema?: z.ZodTypeAny;
}): WorkflowChain<INPUT_SCHEMA, RESULT_SCHEMA, NEW_DATA, ...>
```

Data type flows through: the return type of `execute` becomes `CURRENT_DATA` for the next step. If `outputSchema` is provided, its inferred type is used. If `inputSchema` is provided, it overrides the incoming `data` type.

### Example

```ts
createWorkflowChain({ id: "wf", name: "Wf", input: z.object({ name: z.string() }), result: z.string() })
  .andThen({
    id: "enrich",
    execute: async ({ data }) => {
      // data: { name: string }
      return { ...data, greeting: `Hello ${data.name}` };
    },
  })
  .andThen({
    id: "finalize",
    execute: async ({ data }) => {
      // data: { name: string; greeting: string }
      return data.greeting;
    },
  });
```

